We can get a small amount of insight about the devteam's opinion of
unlimited death drops in general (as opposed to puddings
specificallly) from devteam member Pat Rankin's post in 2001 on a
thread about nerfing XP from regen'd monsters:

"That assumes that gaining experience is the only abusive aspect of
allowing unlimited number of monsters, which is not the case.  It
fails to deal with the issues of corpses (unlimited #offer fodder) and
randomly created objects generated at the time monsters die."



